                                     Project Proposal
                Credit Risk Prediction Using Machine Learning

1. Project Title
Credit Risk Prediction Using Machine Learning Algorithms

2. Introduction
Financial institutions face challenges in determining whether a loan applicant will repay a loan or default. Machine Learning provides a data-driven, accurate, and automated approach to predict credit risk. This project aims to build a model that predicts whether a loan applicant is high-risk or low-risk.

3. Problem Statement
Banks need a reliable way to identify risky customers. Incorrect predictions can cause financial losses. A machine learning model can help reduce these risks.

4. Objectives
- Build a machine learning model to classify applicants as high-risk or low-risk.
- Perform data preprocessing.
- Analyze data through visualizations.
- Train ML models such as Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost.
- Evaluate performance metrics.
- Select the best-performing model.

5. Dataset
Dataset includes:
- Income
- Age
- Credit score
- Loan amount
- Employment length
- Previous defaults
- Debt-to-income ratio
Dataset Link: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/laotse/credit-risk-dataset

6. Methodology
Step 1: Data Collection  
Step 2: Data Preprocessing  
Step 3: Exploratory Data Analysis  
Step 4: Model Training  
Step 5: Model Evaluation  
Step 6: Model Selection

7. Tools & Technologies
Python, Google Colab, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, XGBoost, Matplotlib, GitHub.

8. Expected Outcomes
- A trained ML model.
- Full Jupyter notebook.
- Performance metrics and graphs.
- Project uploaded to GitHub with complete documentation.

9. Applications
- Banks
- Microfinance companies
- Credit card companies
- Fraud detection
- Loan approval automation

10. Conclusion
Credit risk prediction is a major financial sector application. This project helps build a reliable system to reduce loan losses and improve decision making.

